+# Draft memory boundary fixture for #24
+
+This offline fixture follows the maintainer's invitation to use mocks around `db.py` or `app.py`.
+Source baseline: `b0451ca732d5969cb5195f330ee9559805d73f4f`.
+It adds tests and this case card; production files and schema stay unchanged.
+
+From the repository root, using Python 3.10 or newer:
+
+```sh
+python -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_memory_contract.py -v
+```
+
+Only the standard library is needed. The tests import the actual `db.py` with controlled `dotenv` and `asyncpg` import/driver stubs. Dotenv files are not loaded, pool creation is forbidden, and text writes use an automatically cleaned new temporary directory. Caller dependency modules are restored after each import. No server, database, model, API credential or frontend setup is needed.
+
+## Original contract and present coverage
+
+| Proposed boundary | Draft observation | Remaining requirement |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Save A, correct the same logical document to B, query the former decision | Actual `save_memory_chunk` calls use the same `doc_id`; current content/vector bindings and temporary file change. Actual `query_similar_memories` returns the fake driver's current row for the same supplied query vector. | The caller supplies stable document identity. This does not establish a user-facing correction API or whether an old textual name embeds usefully. |
+| Repeat after janitor/re-index and inspect retained history | Pending: no supported janitor/re-index operation or correction-history reader was identified in the reviewed `db.py` / `app.py` entry points. | Exercise a real supported operation and history reader when available. The fixture does not invent either or claim history survives an overwrite. |
+| Competing similar decision in another scope | Actual query SQL and arguments retain the session predicate before the fake driver's ranking/limit. A session-B fixture would rank above the session-A result globally. | PostgreSQL execution and application mapping from projects to sessions require separate checks. Mimir session namespaces are not automatically remember-dammit project scopes. |
+
+## What a passing test means
+
+The recording driver models only the fixture row effects. It checks the declared upsert, session predicate, order and parameter bindings, then computes deterministic cosine ranking over fixed 384-dimensional vectors. It is not a SQL parser or PostgreSQL implementation. Unsupported statements and NULL-vector retrieval are rejected explicitly; pruning behavior is not silently supplied by the fake.
+
+The suite varies content, vectors, sessions and query limits, checks dictionary conversion from read-only driver mappings, and covers uninitialized-pool behavior. Driver statements and bindings are checked independently of the returned rows. These are Python/SQL interaction and temporary-file checks, not a database, concurrency, authorization or semantic-retrieval certification.
+
+Real pgvector execution, embeddings, FastAPI lifecycle/HTTP behavior, pruning, history retention and native-agent use are not checked. The Docker/backend-linkage check requested by `CONTRIBUTING.md` is also not established by this mock suite. A green unit run does not complete #24 or the full shared three-case contract.
